<title>GERMANY: German union urges no gov't cuts in construction.</title>
<headline>German union urges no gov't cuts in construction.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Any attempts by the Bonn government to cut back on public construction programmes as part of its budget savings plan would have a negative effect on employment, German construction union IG Bau warned on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Budgetary consolidation efforts by the government at the current stage in the economic cycle could have the opposite effect to their intended aims,&quot; said IG Bau chairman Klaus Wiesehuegel in a speech on Thursday evening.</p>
<p>The simultaneous trend of lowering wages was hitting consumer demand, Wiesehuegel said, and he forecast a slowdown in the building economy of three percent.</p>
<p>Wiesehuegel said he had no comment on employee demands on pay talks for 1997.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
